.md
# System Modeler in WLJS

Modelica models from Wolfram System Modeler 15.0, simulated in the WLJS notebook's Wolfram kernel (no System Modeler window). Part of [wljs-agent-skills](https://github.com/ptown16801-lang/wljs-agent-skills). The kernel runs with internet off.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# System Modeler in WLJS

Modelica models from Wolfram System Modeler 15.0, simulated in the WLJS notebook's Wolfram kernel (no System Modeler window). Part of [wljs-agent-skills](https://github.com/ptown16801-lang/wljs-agent-skills). The kernel runs with internet off.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
circuit`sim = SystemModelSimulate["IntroductoryExamples.ComponentBased.ElectricCircuit", 10];
SystemModelPlot[circuit`sim, {"inductor1.i", "capacitor1.v"}, PlotRange -> All, PlotLegends -> {"inductor current (A)", "capacitor voltage (V)"}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["F05f7865e-6176-4164-a5e4-9aedb2527a73"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[PointSize[1/180], RGBColor[0.24, 0.6, 0.8], AbsoluteThickness[2]], Directive[PointSize[1/180], RGBColor[0.95, 0.627, 0.1425], AbsoluteThickness[2]]}, {"inductor current (A)", "capacitor voltage (V)"}, LegendMarkers -> {{False, Automatic}, {False, Automatic}}, Joined -> {True, True}, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], After, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Parameter sweep
The same circuit with three values of `resistor1.R`, each a separate simulation; the results come back as Wolfram Language data.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Parameter sweep
The same circuit with three values of `resistor1.R`, each a separate simulation; the results come back as Wolfram Language data.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
circuit`sweep = Table[SystemModelSimulate["IntroductoryExamples.ComponentBased.ElectricCircuit", 10, <|"ParameterValues" -> {"resistor1.R" -> r}|>], {r, {1, 10, 100}}];
Plot[Evaluate[#["capacitor1.v"][t] & /@ circuit`sweep], {t, 0, 10}, PlotRange -> All, PlotLegends -> {"R1 = 1 Ω", "R1 = 10 Ω", "R1 = 100 Ω"}, AxesLabel -> {"t (s)", "capacitor voltage (V)"}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["F48a3f946-d852-45d0-bf98-a270c267bd44"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.24, 0.6, 0.8], AbsoluteThickness[2]], Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.95, 0.627, 0.1425], AbsoluteThickness[2]], Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.455, 0.7, 0.21], AbsoluteThickness[2]]}, {"R1 = 1 \[CapitalOmega]", "R1 = 10 \[CapitalOmega]", "R1 = 100 \[CapitalOmega]"}, LegendMarkers -> None, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], After, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
